# Panel 186 R7, lane land186, 2026-10-02: a group's record over a C union is
# built naming exactly one member of each union, so a construction may name
# fewer fields than the record declares, and `check` holds only its labels
# (`selfhost/check/group_fields.hero`); what it leaves out is `build`'s.
#
# An argument with no label is told with every field it may be, the fields
# between the ones named before and after it that could take its value: here
# `f`, since `i` cannot take `1.5`. Offered as a guess, since a construction
# that names only some fields has no position that settles which one.

extern "ffi-a-construction.h"
    record SA
        kind: i32
        i: i32
        f: f32
        x: i32
    function sa_x(s: SA) -> i32

function main()
    b = SA(kind: 2, 1.5, x: 4)  #~ missing_label
    print(sa_x(b))
